    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460">

                <pb facs="0483" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg463"/>

                <head>Mr. Pruyn to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Kanagawa,
                            Yokohama</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 1, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The government have agreed to pay the sum
                    of $10,000, being the bill of damages presented by Russell &amp; Co., for the
                    interruption of the voyage of the Pembroke.</p>
                <p>Satsuma has not paid British indemnity, though eight days overdue; explanations
                    have been asked from Gorogio.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
